    pr_ref:  # 0265
    description: "Follow-up to WI-gafog (PR #3357 — Python module-level constants\nindexed as variable Symbols). The new variable Symbols are produced\ncorrectly, but `from X import BAR` statements don't emit any edge to\nthe imported BAR Symbol, so the imported-and-used constants appear as\norphan nodes in the graph.\n\n## Symptom (observed 2026-04-25 self-analysis)\n\n- Total python `variable` Symbols: 1,315 (1,132 ALL_CAPS constants).\n- Orphan `variable` nodes (no in, no out): 1,171.\n- Net effect: graph orphan rate jumped 1.0% → 4.9% between\n  v2.5.1 (2026-04-05 baseline) and v2.7.0 (today), almost entirely\n  driven by these new orphans.\n\nThe constants ARE being imported and used at import sites — for\nexample `PASS_VERSION` is referenced by every analyzer module — but\nthe analyzer's import-resolution pass only looks up function and\nclass symbols, not `variable`-kind symbols.\n\n## Recommended fix\n\nExtend Python's import-resolution pass (in\n`packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py`,\nin the `_process_import` / cross-file binding-resolution code path)\nso that `from <mod> import <NAME>`:\n\n1. Looks up `<NAME>` in the global symbol registry across all kinds\n   (function, class, **variable**, …) — currently restricted.\n2. When `<NAME>` resolves to a `variable`-kind symbol, emits a\n   `references` edge from the importing module/file to the variable\n   Symbol with `evidence_type='ast_import_reference'`.\n3. Also handles bare attribute access at use sites — `mod.CONSTANT`\n   should emit a `references` edge to the variable.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAfter this lands:\n\n- Self-analysis dogfood: orphan `variable` count drops from ~1,171 to\n  near zero (modulo genuinely-exported-but-internally-unused constants\n  like `__all__` entries that are only consumed by external code).\n- Overall orphan rate returns toward the v2.5.1 1.0% baseline (within\n  ~0.5pp).\n- New regression test: a fixture with `module1.py` defining\n  `CONSTANT = 1` and `module2.py` doing `from module1 import CONSTANT`\n  — assert a `references` edge from module2 to the CONSTANT Symbol.\n\n## Validation\n\n1. `pytest` — green, 100% coverage on changed files.\n2. Self-analysis dogfood: orphan-rate metric drops back near baseline.\n3. Tag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time. Claim: \"Python\n   constant import-reference recovery reduces orphan-variable count\n   on the bakeoff corpus and improves centrality ranking signal for\n   shared-constants modules.\"\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Type-narrowing import resolution (e.g. `from X import Y` where Y is\n  a class or function — those already work).\n- Star-imports (`from X import *`) — separate (and harder) problem.\n- Cross-language constant references — Python-only for this item.\n- Promoting \"used by N importers\" into the centrality ranking\n  weighting — a separate enrichment item once the references edges\n  exist.\n\n## Relationship to WI-gafog (PR #3357)\n\nWI-gafog made the variables visible. This item makes them connected.\nOnce both land, module-level constants participate in the call graph\nthe same way functions and classes do."  # 0265
    fields: {}  # 0265
- op: update  # 0b1c
  at: '2026-04-25T09:00:23Z'  # 0b1c
  by: agent  # 0b1c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0b1c
  clock: 2  # 0b1c
  nonce: 0b1c  # 0b1c
  set:  # 0b1c
    description: "**REVISED 2026-04-25 after empirical verification.** The original\nframing of this WI conflated two separate gaps. Verification on the\npost-WI-zujip self-analysis output revealed:\n\n## What's already working\n\n- **Cross-file `from X import BAR` for variable Symbols**: the\n  `_extract_import_edges` pass at\n  `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py:1714`\n  already calls `_lookup_symbol_by_module` without a kind filter,\n  already finds variable-kind Symbols, and already emits an `imports`\n  edge whose `dst` points at the actual variable Symbol id. Verified\n  example: the `imports` edge for `from ir import PASS_VERSION` lands\n  at `dst='python:packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:42-42:PASS_VERSION:variable'`\n  — the real Symbol, not a synthesized boundary.\n- The reason it LOOKS like an in-degree of 1 instead of N is Plan A's\n  src-side collapse + tuple-dedup: every importer's `imports` edge has\n  `src=make_file_id(file)` which canonicalises to\n  `python:<external>:0-0:file:file`, then (canonical, BAR, \"imports\")\n  collapses across all importers. **WI-ramuv reverses this** —\n  importer-count attribution gets restored once file Symbols are real.\n\n## What is NOT working (the real gap)\n\n**Intra-file bare-name reads of module-level constants don't emit\nedges.** The 1,171 orphan `variable` Symbols on hypergumbo\nself-analysis are constants that have no cross-file importer at all\n— they're defined and read entirely WITHIN their own module. Three\nverified examples:\n\n| Symbol | Defined | Read |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ANDROID_MANIFEST` | `xml_config.py:58` | `xml_config.py:474` (`if path.name == ANDROID_MANIFEST`) |\n| `APEX_BUILTINS` | `apex.py:55` | `apex.py:658, 695` |\n| `PASS_ID` | various | same-file uses inside class methods (e.g. `dependency.py:123, 164`) |\n\nThe Python analyzer's symbol-extraction pass walks function/method\nbodies for `ast.Call` (call edges) and class definitions, but does NOT\nwalk for `ast.Name` reads that resolve to module-level constants in\nthe same file. Adding this resolution is the actual fix for the\norphan-rate metric.\n\n## Two distinct deliverables (recommend splitting)\n\n### Deliverable A — semantic refinement (~2 hr, low metric impact)\n\nChange `_extract_import_edges` to additionally emit a `references`\nedge (alongside or instead of `imports`) when the resolved Symbol's\nkind is `variable`. Captures the semantic intent — `from X import BAR`\nwhere BAR is data is not the same as `from X import func` where func\nis callable. Won't move the orphan-rate metric (cross-file imports\nalready work). Probably NOT worth doing in isolation. Worth doing as\npart of WI-ramuv (which restores per-file attribution and naturally\nre-prompts thinking about what edge type fits).\n\n### Deliverable B — intra-file reference resolution (~half day, real metric impact)\n\nExtend the Python analyzer's symbol-extraction pass to walk function\nand method bodies for `ast.Name` reads. For each name read:\n\n1. Check if the name resolves to a module-level constant defined in\n   the same file (build a per-file constant table at extraction time,\n   keyed by name).\n2. If so, emit a `references` edge from the enclosing\n   function/method Symbol to the variable Symbol with\n   `evidence_type='ast_name_read'` and `confidence=0.85`.\n\nSkips reads that shadow the module-level name (function-local\n`PASS_ID = ...` would not emit). Class-level attribute references\n(`self.X` for self-typed reads) are out of scope for v1.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Self-analysis dogfood: orphan `variable` Symbol count drops from\n  1,171 to near zero (modulo genuinely export-only constants like\n  `ANALYZER_MODULES` re-exported via `__all__` with no intra-file\n  reader).\n- Overall orphan rate returns toward the v2.5.1 1.0% baseline (within\n  ~0.5pp).\n- Cross-file imports continue to work (regression guard).\n\n### Sequencing\n\nRecommend doing Deliverable B first (real metric impact), then folding\nA into WI-ramuv when it lands (semantic refinement makes more sense\nonce per-file attribution is restored). If only one ships, B is the\none that matters.\n\n## Status\n\n`todo_soft` — design is now clear after 2026-04-25 dogfood; awaiting\nhuman prioritization. The design discussion in this description\nsupersedes the original framing.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Star-imports (`from X import *`) — separate (and harder) problem.\n- Cross-language constant references — Python-only for this item.\n- Bare-attribute reads of OTHER modules' constants\n  (`other_module.CONSTANT`) — already partially handled by\n  `_emit_module_attr_refs` (`module_attr_ref` edge type, not\n  `references`). Generalizing it to emit `references` for variable\n  Symbols too would be a Deliverable A bolt-on.\n- Promoting \"used by N readers\" into the centrality ranking weighting\n  — a separate enrichment item once the references edges exist.\n- Function-local name resolution beyond the module scope.\n\n## Validation\n\nRun hypergumbo on itself before/after the Deliverable B change. The\norphan-rate metric is the primary signal:\n- pre-fix:  4.9% (1,441 orphans / 29,280 nodes), 1,171 variable orphans\n- target:  ~1.0% (matching 2026-04-05 baseline before WI-gafog)\n\nTag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time. Claim: \"Python\nintra-file constant-read resolution emits ~5,000+ new `references`\nedges on the bakeoff corpus and reduces orphan-variable count by\n≥80%.\"\n\n## Relationship to WI-gafog (PR #3357)\n\nWI-gafog made the variables visible. This item makes them connected\nWITHIN their own module. WI-ramuv would make their CROSS-module\nattribution complete (restoring the per-importer count that's\ncurrently collapsed)."  # 0b1c
